G2908.def:
**κρείσσων**
(Epic and old Att..) and κρείττων (later Att..), prop. comparat. of κρατύς, strong, but in sense often (as in cl., see LS, see word) as comparat. of ἀγαθός, [in LXX chiefly for טוֹב ;]
**better**;
(a) **as to ad­vantage or usefulness**: [[1Co.11.17|1Co.11:17]], [[Heb.11.40; 12.24|Heb.11:40 12:24]]; πολλῷ μᾶλλον κ., [[Php.1.23|Php.1:23]] κρεῖσσον ποιεῖν, [[1Co.7.38|1Co.7:38]] ἐστιν, before inf., [[1Co.7.9|1Co.7:9]], [[2Pe.2.21|2Pe.2:21]];
(b) **as to excellence**: [[Heb.1.4; 6.9; 7.7, 19; 7.22; 8.6; 9.23; 10.34; 11.16, 35|Heb.1:4 6:9 7:7, 19 7:22 8:6 9:23 10:34 11:16, 35]]; κ. ἐστι, before inf., [[1Pe.3.17|1Pe.3:17]]†
(AS)
